\title{Seemingly Unrelated Estimation for Model Comparisons}
\description{
The \code{suest} package combines two or more separately fitted regression
models into a single object with a joint model-robust covariance
matrix. The combined object works with the
\href{https://marginaleffects.com/}{marginaleffects package} to compare
predictions, slopes, and average comparisons across models.
}
\section{Supported models}{

\code{lm()}, binary logit, probit, and complementary-log-log models fitted by
\code{glm()} or \code{glm2::glm2()}, Poisson and other supported GLMs,
negative-binomial models fitted by \code{\link[MASS:glm.nb]{MASS::glm.nb()}}, ordered logit and
probit models fitted by \code{\link[MASS:polr]{MASS::polr()}} or restricted \code{ordinal::clm()}
specifications, multinomial logit models fitted by \code{\link[nnet:multinom]{nnet::multinom()}}, and
parametric survival or censored-regression models fitted by
\code{survival::survreg()}, and beta regressions fitted by \code{betareg::betareg()}.
Poisson and negative-binomial zero-inflated models fitted by
\code{pscl::zeroinfl()} are also supported.
Truncated Gaussian regressions fitted by \code{truncreg::truncreg()} are
supported as well, as are direct Tobit models fitted by
\code{censReg::censReg()} and unweighted two-stage least squares fitted by
\code{fixest::feols()} without absorbed fixed effects. Heteroskedastic binary
probit and logit fitted by \code{Rchoice::hetprob()} are supported.
Maximum-likelihood IV probit fitted by \code{Rchoice::ivpml()} and bivariate
probit fitted by \code{mvProbit::mvProbit()} are supported with their documented
adapter restrictions.
Unweighted individual fixed-effects, between-effects, and Swamy-Arora
random-effects linear panel models fitted by \code{plm::plm()} are supported;
unbalanced random-effects fits can retain small engine-specific differences.
Single-level random-intercept Gaussian models fitted by \code{nlme::lme()} with
\code{method = "ML"} are supported, including both variance components.
Unweighted individual random-intercept binary logit/probit and gamma
random-effects Poisson models fitted by \code{pglm::pglm()} are supported under
the restrictions documented in \code{\link[=suest]{suest()}}.
Unweighted binomial-logit, Poisson-log, and negative-binomial NB2 log models fitted by
\code{glmmTMB::glmmTMB()} with one conditional random intercept are supported
under the restrictions documented in \code{\link[=suest]{suest()}}.
Unweighted GEE fitted by \code{geepack::geeglm()} is supported for Gaussian
identity, binary logit/probit/cloglog, and Poisson log models with
independence or exchangeable correlation.
Explicit \code{weight_type = "pweight"} support is available for the model
families corresponding to Stata \code{suest2}'s ordinary pweight route.
Joint cluster-robust covariance is available through the \code{cluster} argument
to \code{\link[=suest]{suest()}}.
Compatible systems fitted in multiple imputed datasets can be pooled with
\code{\link[=suest_mi]{suest_mi()}} using Rubin's rules. The initial MI interface supports joint
coefficients, covariance, summaries, and coefficient-level hypotheses.
}

